# Markdown Contents Section

Each Markdown document carries its own navigation index, named `## Contents`, so a reader
can jump straight to a section.

## Rules

- **Name**: `## Contents`. Do **not** call it `Summary` — the per-changelist reports under
  `WorkDoneByChangelists/P4-History/` already use `## Summary` for a prose summary of the
  changelist.
- **Position**: after the `Parent:` line, the `#` title and the intro paragraph, and
  **before** the first `##` section (above the horizontal rule when there is one).
- **Depth**: list `##` and `###` headings, `###` indented by two spaces. Ignore `####` and
  deeper, and ignore `#` lines inside fenced code blocks.
- **Skip short documents**: fewer than three `##` sections means nothing to navigate — no
  Contents section. This is why the per-changelist reports have none.
- **Keep it in sync**: when you add, rename, remove or reorder a heading, update the
  Contents list of that document in the same commit.

## Anchor format

GitHub slugs: drop the markup (backticks, bold, link syntax), delete punctuation
**without replacing it**, lowercase, then turn every remaining space into a hyphen. A
deleted `—`, `&` or `/` between two spaces therefore leaves a **double** hyphen. Repeated
headings get `-1`, `-2`, … suffixes.

| Heading | Anchor |
|---------|--------|
| `## Builders & commandlets` | `#builders--commandlets` |
| `## Pass / Fail Criteria` | `#pass--fail-criteria` |
| `### Config location & key settings` | `#config-location--key-settings` |
| second `### Parameters` in the file | `#parameters-1` |

## Example

```markdown
Parent: [Reference Docs](README.md)

# Environment & infrastructure

Cross-cutting environment and build-infra notes.

## Contents

- [Actor Folders — the format & the engine patches](#actor-folders--the-format--the-engine-patches)
- [Related changelists](#related-changelists)
- [See also](#see-also)

---

## Actor Folders — the format & the engine patches
```
